                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Whelp, had this one for ages, and it was ok. Be prepared for a somewhat ghetto and short walking simulator with light horror elements, but some actually decent puzzles and environments. There were quite a few bugs here including my directional movement getting stuck a couple times, UE4 shenanigans including the 62fps cap and encrypted configs (not worth it to bypass, but there are tools available for this), and I dodged a softlock by glancing at a guide. \n\nOverall though, I think this is fine and actually exceeded my expectations a bit, or at least met them considering I got this for $2 and it appears to be the first game from a duo of devs. I'm not sure I'd go out of my way to play this, but if you like quick walking simulators, this one actually had a few puzzles and beat out some of the other games in this same tier I've played this Halloween season.  This took me about 2 hours or so to beat, so I think maybe $3 (the regular sale price) would be my recommended target for this if you have interest. Factoring for the price I paid I'd give it a 6/10. Seems like a decent amount of effort went into this, even if seems like it may be somewhat of an asset flip.",
